;; verified-derives — a verified claim must derive from at least one source-span
;; (REQ-KG-003 / REQ-KG-012).
;;
;; Booklogic port of the tbf:ClaimShape sh:sparql constraint in
;; assets/shapes.ttl:
;;   SELECT $this WHERE {
;;     $this tbf:status "verified" .
;;     FILTER NOT EXISTS { $this prov:wasDerivedFrom ?src . }
;;   }
;;
;; The :where binds the claim id (?focus) and pins status = "verified"; the :not
;; negates a source-span joined on the claim id (the relational form of
;; ?claim prov:wasDerivedFrom ?src). ?focus is bound positive and threaded into
;; the negation, so this is a safe inline Cozo negation. A verified claim with no
;; source-span fires; a proposed claim is out of scope; a verified claim with a
;; span conforms.
;;
;; The :message and :path are taken EXACTLY from the sh:sparql shape and the C0.2
;; golden (tests/golden/kg/shacl_report_violating.json): the sh:sparql node has
;; an sh:message but no sh:path, so pyshacl reports an empty path "".
;;
;; DIVERGENCE (mirrors assets/kg-queries/unsupported_claims.edn): the .rq negates
;; prov:wasDerivedFrom, which the RDF projector emits for BOTH source spans and
;; derived_from claim refs; this port negates only the source-span back-ref.
;; Reconcile at P5 cutover.
(defconstraint :verified-derives
  :message "Verified claims must derive from at least one source-span entity."
  :path ""
  :where [[?c :claim/id ?focus]
          [?c :claim/status "verified"]]
  :not   [[?s :source-span/claim-id ?focus]])
